---

## 1. System Overview

{{ project_name }} is a Battery Management System for HV battery pack monitoring,
cell balancing, and safety protection. Built on NXP {{ mcu }} with ASIL {{ asil_label }}.

---

## 2. Voltage Monitoring

### BMS-VLT-001: Cell Voltage Measurement
- The system SHALL measure each cell voltage with ±2 mV accuracy at 10 ms intervals
- The system SHALL support up to 96 series cells via analog front-end IC
- The system SHALL detect cell overvoltage (> 4.2 V) within 20 ms

### BMS-VLT-002: Voltage Validation
- The system SHALL validate cell voltage using two independent AFE measurements
- The system SHALL detect AFE communication errors via CRC check
- The system SHALL report voltage sensor plausibility faults as DTC

---

## 3. Temperature Monitoring

### BMS-TMP-001: Temperature Measurement
- The system SHALL measure up to 16 NTC temperature sensors across the battery pack
- The system SHALL sample all temperature channels every 100 ms
- The system SHALL detect overtemperature (> 60°C cell) within 100 ms

### BMS-TMP-002: Thermal Runaway Detection
- The system SHALL detect rapid temperature rise (> 5°C/s) as potential thermal runaway
- The system SHALL trigger contactor open on thermal runaway detection
- The system SHALL report thermal event via CAN within 50 ms

---

## 4. Current Monitoring

### BMS-CUR-001: Current Sensor Interface
- The system SHALL measure battery pack current via shunt-based sensor
- The system SHALL support bidirectional current measurement (±500 A range)
- The system SHALL sample current every 1 ms for coulomb counting

### BMS-CUR-002: Overcurrent Protection
- The system SHALL detect discharge overcurrent (> 300 A) within 1 ms
- The system SHALL detect charge overcurrent (> 200 A) within 1 ms
- The system SHALL open contactors on overcurrent events

---

## 5. Cell Balancing

### BMS-BAL-001: Passive Balancing
- The system SHALL perform passive balancing via bleed resistors (100 mA per cell)
- The system SHALL activate balancing when cell voltage delta exceeds 20 mV
- The system SHALL limit balancing time to prevent overheating

### BMS-BAL-002: Balancing Strategy
- The system SHALL balance during charge phase (CC/CV)
- The system SHALL prioritize cells with highest voltage deviation
- The system SHALL report balancing status per cell on CAN

---

## 6. SOC/SOH Estimation

### BMS-SOC-001: State of Charge
- The system SHALL compute SOC using coulomb counting + voltage correction
- The system SHALL update SOC every 100 ms with ±3% accuracy
- The system SHALL recalibrate SOC at full charge (100%) and deep discharge (0%)

### BMS-SOH-001: State of Health
- The system SHALL track capacity fade as primary SOH indicator
- The system SHALL update SOH after each full charge-discharge cycle
- The system SHALL report SOH < 80% as end-of-life warning

---

## 7. Safety Requirements (ASIL D)

### BMS-SAF-001: Contactors Control (ASIL D)
- The system SHALL control at least three contactors: Positive, Negative, and Precharge
- The system SHALL verify contactor state via auxiliary feedback contacts
- The system SHALL open all contactors within 10 ms of any safety violation
- The system SHALL detect contactor welding via voltage sense after open command

### BMS-SAF-002: Insulation Monitoring
- The system SHALL monitor HV-to-chassis insulation resistance
- The system SHALL detect insulation fault when resistance < 500 Ω/V
- The system SHALL open contactors on insulation fault

### BMS-SAF-003: Redundant Voltage Monitoring
- The system SHALL implement two independent voltage monitoring paths
- The system SHALL enter safe state if voltage paths disagree > 5%
- The system SHALL use E2E protection for all safety-critical CAN signals

---

## 8. Acceptance Scenarios

### Scenario: Overvoltage Detection
- GIVEN cell voltage > 4.2 V threshold
- WHEN the measurement is validated
- THEN the system SHALL open all contactors within 20 ms
- AND SHALL set DTC for cell overvoltage

### Scenario: Thermal Event
- GIVEN cell temperature rises at 6°C/s
- WHEN thermal runaway is detected
- THEN contactors SHALL open within 10 ms
- AND a thermal event warning SHALL be broadcast on CAN

### Scenario: Contactor Welding Detection
- GIVEN contactor positive is commanded open
- WHEN pack voltage > 50 V is still measured at inverter side
- THEN the system SHALL detect contactor welding
- AND SHALL set DTC_CONTACTOR_WELDED
